// Card and container metadata for the HR Policy Navigator (HRPN) architecture scenes.
//
// Same model as the D2D Focus dossier (airbus-genair-d2d docs/d2d-decision/focus/scene-metadata.js),
// re-authored here (no runtime import of d2d files): card template A (460 x 200),
// BOX for containers, zone layout { north, south, southUnder, fill, flows }.
//
// Card text rules (chain/ServiceNode.svelte): role <= 2 segments of <= 2 words,
// the code appears once and never inside the name, short name and detail
// (one 24 px line each inside the 460 px card).
//
// Evidence classes: `declared` = present and wired in the code read (HRPN main @667529f);
// `dormant` = present but not reached (no consumer, variable unset, not called);
// `external` = third-party / platform service or a cited source document (not code of this repo);
// `target` = required by a cited source (BRD, ARD, ARB) and not built;
// `hypothesis` = option-3 assumption drawn from a cited platform document;
// `unknown` = not verified.
// Runtime states: no deployment was observed by this session, so wired items are `unknown`,
// unwired ones `dormant`, manual steps `manual`, target and hypothesis items `not-applicable`.
// Deployed-state check of 2026-10-19 (read-only gcloud, `DS` below) is cited in `ev` of the cards it confirms
// (SUB, RUNZ, RAG, AEAPP); evidence classes and runtime states are left unchanged.
//
// Tints (owner rule for HRPN): `genair` = native GenAiR template / Cutter / AgentGarden code
// (files created by the "Created with GenAiR-cutter" commits 66b64ed and 6a16d08);
// `specific` = HRPN-specific code (commits after 6a16d08, 2026-09-25 -> 2026-10-12);
// `added` = target addition needed (new or changed); `removed` = to remove in the target;
// `risk` = present but weak or at risk (red frame); none = Google / third-party managed service.
// Decided target S2-target (owner rule 2026-10-22): `genair` = GenAiR standard (blue); `custom` = customisation within the
// GenAiR template frame, data services included (green); `outside` = added outside the frame (yellow); none = managed service.
// A wrapping box (BOX) may carry a tint too: the colour of the box when folded.
//
// Every card and container carries `ev`: evidence references checked by build-scenes.mjs.
// Formats: `path:L`, `path:L1-L2`, `path:L1,L2` (path relative to the repo root, or `~/...`);
// `git:<sha>` (commit of this repo); `doc:<text>` (external documentation, not verifiable offline).

const EVIDENCE = new Set(['observed', 'declared', 'dormant', 'external', 'target', 'hypothesis', 'unknown']);
const RUNTIME = new Set(['active', 'dormant', 'manual', 'unknown', 'not-applicable']);
export const TINTS = new Set(['genair', 'specific', 'added', 'removed', 'risk', 'custom', 'outside']);

const roleSegments = role => role.split('·').map(part => part.trim()).filter(Boolean);
export const roleIsShort = role => {
  const segments = roleSegments(role);
  return segments.length > 0 && segments.length <= 2 && segments.every(part => part.split(/\s+/).length <= 2);
};

